if {guard_introduced} == false:
	set {guard_introduced} = true
	join detective right
	detective: Greetings. I'm here to investigate the recent murder of Count Dracula.
	detective: Tell me about yourself.
	join guard left
	guard: I'm a guard.
	guard: ...
	detective: ...
	guard: ...
	guard: Fine.
	guard: I was hired to guard for this dinner party Dracula was having.
	guard: I've been doing this sort of work a while. I tend to bounce around between estates. Keeps the monotony from getting to my head.
	guard: At least I'm not stuck here long term like those other guys.
	guard: Been a while since the last time I guarded for a vampire's event. They're strange folk aren't they?
	detective: What can you tell me about the events of the murder?
	guard: Not much, to be honest.
	guard: I remained outside the whole time, as a guard is meant to.
	guard: As the party was getting close to ending, before all the drama unfolded, Dracula brought me inside for a brief tour around the place.
	guard: But I went right back to my post afterward.
	guard: At one point the cook, Camelia, came outside to talk to me. She told me that Count Dracula had collapsed at the dining table.
	guard: We talked for a bit after that, then she went back inside.
	guard: ...
	guard: I was eventually brought inside to address an argument that had started between Camelia and one of the other vampire guests, Aslan I think it was.
	guard: Aslan was trying to blame Camelia for what happend to Dracula.
	guard (angry): I wish I could have helped Camelia, but I honestly wasn't sure what to say.
	guard (speaking): The other vampire, Narin, seemed pretty tired of it too, so I decided we should both head upstairs to check on Dracula.
	guard: That's when we found him stabbed dead with a stake in his bedroom.
	guard: Honestly, though, I'd be careful about Narin. The look on her face made me feel almost like she wasn't surprised, like she had already known he was dead.
else:
	join guard left
guard: ...
- Question
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"present_evidence":"guard"}"]
- Leave
